dsv41 patch 0034: backport of vLLM PR #59894 ("trim the last KV-source layer in decoder replay"), eager path only.
Base: vLLM 6e517b15 + sudoingX patches 0001-0021 (sudoingX v1.1). Layer 20 (the last KV source, compress ratio 1, candidate
source) used to run on ALL rows in replay steps although the trimmed rows only need its KV. Now it writes every row's KV
and then runs as the first replay layer on the replay rows only. Same windows and KV visibility as before; not
guaranteed bit-exact (layer 20 now runs with the small replay row count, i.e. other EXL3 kernel paths).
Measured on 2x GB10 together with 0035/0036 at 2000 MHz: 18.5K TTFT 9.04 -> 8.42 s, 314K prefill 171 -> 152 s, decode
unchanged; cold-prefill A/B 5/5 identical texts (mean |dlogp| 0.009 vs 0.006 noise), corruption test 0 hits; unit tests 11/11.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_REPLAY_TRIM_CUT=0 restores the old path.

